WEBVTT

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.835
[shivering]

00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:14.099
Mom, you sure
you don't want to join us?

00:00:14.273 --> 00:00:15.318
It's really warm in here.

00:00:15.492 --> 00:00:18.060
Uh, I'm not really
a sleep-pile person.

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:20.236
-I have a shawl to keep me...
-[wind gusts]

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.367
warm.

00:00:21.541 --> 00:00:22.499
That's okay.

00:00:22.673 --> 00:00:24.675
I'll just use the travel basket

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:25.806
-to shield my...
-[wind gusts, basket tumbles]

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.939
Ah! Come on!

00:00:29.245 --> 00:00:30.072
[screams]

00:00:30.246 --> 00:00:32.422
[gasping]

00:00:32.596 --> 00:00:34.772
[muffled gasping, grunting]

00:00:34.946 --> 00:00:36.904
[panting]

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:39.820
-It's cozy, isn't it?
-[others snoring]

00:00:39.994 --> 00:00:41.779
Told ya.

00:00:41.953 --> 00:00:43.302
[Hope sighs]

00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:47.567
Hey, um, Ugga?

00:00:47.741 --> 00:00:48.612
Hmm?

00:00:48.786 --> 00:00:50.092
-Eep?
-Hmm?

00:00:50.266 --> 00:00:52.181
Hi.

00:00:52.355 --> 00:00:55.184
I just want to say, um...

00:00:55.358 --> 00:00:57.229
that I have been terrible.

00:00:57.403 --> 00:01:01.712
After everything I did and said,

00:01:01.886 --> 00:01:03.801
you still saved me.

00:01:03.975 --> 00:01:05.368
Why?

00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:08.458
Well, we always say
the pack stays together.

00:01:08.632 --> 00:01:10.199
Unofficial motto.

00:01:10.373 --> 00:01:11.591
It's okay.

00:01:11.765 --> 00:01:13.332
No.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.725
It is not okay.

00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:16.335
I was awful.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.120
-It's fine.
-I tried to steal Guy from you.

00:01:18.294 --> 00:01:19.947
-It's okay.
-And I gave you

00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:22.211
a-a passive-aggressive basket.

00:01:22.385 --> 00:01:24.952
-Yeah, that was weird.
-Who does that?

00:01:25.127 --> 00:01:30.044
And your daughter, obviously,
is not a rat baby.

00:01:30.219 --> 00:01:31.481
She's beautiful.

00:01:31.655 --> 00:01:35.746
She is a beautiful...
human baby.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.009
-And...
-GRAN: Enough.

00:01:39.315 --> 00:01:42.144
♪ ♪

00:01:47.018 --> 00:01:48.324
Where's Guy?

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.154
-I think I'm his new pet.
-[growls]

00:01:52.328 --> 00:01:54.547
Oh. That's rough.

00:01:54.721 --> 00:01:57.594
[whooping wildly]

00:01:57.768 --> 00:01:59.030
What's he saying, Guy?

00:01:59.204 --> 00:02:01.815
The aged wise one has decreed,
[grunts]

00:02:01.989 --> 00:02:04.427
because we have
no bananas for the monster,

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:07.038
[grunting]:
you will be...

00:02:07.212 --> 00:02:09.649
I think I can translate
from here, Guy.

00:02:09.823 --> 00:02:13.087
They're saying
the oafish caveman

00:02:13.262 --> 00:02:15.177
will grow bananas for them,

00:02:15.351 --> 00:02:17.744
watering the fields
with his bitter tears.

00:02:17.918 --> 00:02:19.398
Ooh.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:22.227
And naturally,
they want me to supervise. Hmm.

00:02:22.401 --> 00:02:23.315
Not what they said.

00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:24.925
You can't speak punch monkey.

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:26.927
Can I not?

00:02:27.101 --> 00:02:31.628
Monkeys, I have mastered your
zesty and expressive language.

00:02:31.802 --> 00:02:32.977
GUY:
No, you haven't.

00:02:33.151 --> 00:02:34.892
Let me talk
a little punch monkey.

00:02:35.066 --> 00:02:37.982
Phil Betterman is so smart,
he's stupid!

00:02:38.156 --> 00:02:41.507
Oh. What do you have to say
to this witty rejoinder?

00:02:41.681 --> 00:02:43.770
[inhales sharply, chuckles]
You know what?

00:02:43.944 --> 00:02:44.858
Let me fix this.

00:02:45.032 --> 00:02:46.077
Do you mind?

00:02:46.251 --> 00:02:48.166
Can I, can I take this? Thanks.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.559
-Do not interrupt me!
-You stop interrupting me!

00:02:49.733 --> 00:02:50.951
Will you two stop it?

00:02:51.125 --> 00:02:52.170
I'm trying to get us
out of this.

00:02:52.344 --> 00:02:53.519
I'm in good with these monkeys.

00:02:53.693 --> 00:02:54.912
I have a job.

00:02:55.086 --> 00:02:56.827
And you two,
you're gonna mess it up.

00:02:57.001 --> 00:02:58.437
Like you mess up everything.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:02.006
Like you messed up my-my
beautiful teenage romance.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.444
[sniffling]

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:09.709
Guy, son, please understand.

00:03:09.883 --> 00:03:12.408
It's Grug's fault.

00:03:12.582 --> 00:03:14.714
-[Grug yells]
-[confused grunting]

00:03:14.888 --> 00:03:17.195
-PHIL: Get him, Guy!
-GUY: I am not on your side!

00:03:17.369 --> 00:03:19.066
-Yeah, he's with me!
-I'm not on yours, either!

00:03:19.241 --> 00:03:20.807
-[Guy yells, grunts]
-PHIL: Ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow...

00:03:20.981 --> 00:03:22.244
[groans]:
Oh.

00:03:23.723 --> 00:03:26.944
I recognize
those broad shoulders.

00:03:27.118 --> 00:03:28.162
Oh, Eep, you came for me.

00:03:28.337 --> 00:03:29.729
-Boop.
-[growls]

00:03:29.903 --> 00:03:31.470
[shudders]

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.690
[Phil and Grug grunting]

00:03:33.864 --> 00:03:34.952
[both yelling]

00:03:35.126 --> 00:03:36.562
[high-pitched screaming]

00:03:36.736 --> 00:03:38.042
[grunting]

00:03:38.216 --> 00:03:41.306
[soft murmuring]

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:42.960
What are you doing?

00:03:43.134 --> 00:03:45.441
GRUG:
[grunts] Where you going, Phil?

00:03:45.615 --> 00:03:47.530
[panting]

00:03:47.704 --> 00:03:50.054
No man cave here.

00:03:50.228 --> 00:03:51.838
[Phil gasps]

00:03:52.012 --> 00:03:54.711
You can hide from your family,
[chuckles]

00:03:54.885 --> 00:03:58.280
but you can't hide from me.

00:03:58.454 --> 00:04:00.020
-[groans]
-[grunts]

00:04:00.194 --> 00:04:04.764
[panting]: Well, your precious
pack is glad you're gone.

00:04:04.938 --> 00:04:06.766
[Grug grunts]

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.420
[straining]:
'Cause you smother them.

00:04:08.594 --> 00:04:10.553
[gasps] Oh.

00:04:10.727 --> 00:04:13.207
-Well, you built a wall
around your family. -[grunts]

00:04:13.382 --> 00:04:18.343
But you also built a wall
around your heart.

00:04:18.517 --> 00:04:19.605
Oh!

00:04:19.779 --> 00:04:21.390
You know what you are?

00:04:21.564 --> 00:04:23.000
I'll tell you what you are.

00:04:23.174 --> 00:04:24.393
-You're...
-A bad...

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:25.568
BOTH:
Father.

00:04:25.742 --> 00:04:26.786
[both gasp]

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.008
[distorted yelling, grunting]

00:04:32.444 --> 00:04:34.751
Words as weapons?

00:04:34.925 --> 00:04:36.274
You're just a cave girl.

00:04:36.448 --> 00:04:38.407
It's called a shower.
Try it.

00:04:38.581 --> 00:04:41.279
I told her to take a shower.
Who does that?

00:04:41.453 --> 00:04:42.846
[laughs]:
You did.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.326
Aw, Eep.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:45.327
[screams]

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:47.111
Congratulations, Phil.

00:04:47.285 --> 00:04:49.505
[panting]:
You hit me where it hurts.

00:04:49.679 --> 00:04:52.203
[panting]:
Likewise.

00:04:52.377 --> 00:04:54.205
GUY [faint, muffled]:
Hey, Phil!

00:04:54.379 --> 00:04:56.381
Hey! Hello, Grug!

00:04:56.555 --> 00:04:58.427
Grug, am I hallucinating?

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:00.559
No.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.344
Guy's a giant banana.

00:05:02.518 --> 00:05:04.520
What the monkeys were trying
to say was that

00:05:04.694 --> 00:05:06.913
we're gonna be sacrificed
to the monster

00:05:07.087 --> 00:05:08.567
at full moon tonight.

00:05:10.134 --> 00:05:11.788
[howling]

00:05:11.962 --> 00:05:14.399
[both howling]

00:05:14.573 --> 00:05:16.662
[Ugga sighs softly]

00:05:16.836 --> 00:05:18.838
She's still waiting out there.

00:05:19.012 --> 00:05:21.580
EEP: I'm not sure
her hair is coming back.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.974
[Belt murmurs sadly]

00:05:24.148 --> 00:05:27.238
[yawning]

00:05:30.372 --> 00:05:31.590
[grunts, sighs]

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.113
[Hope grunts, cracks neck]

00:05:33.287 --> 00:05:34.158
-HOPE: How long was I out for?
-[all gasp]

00:05:34.332 --> 00:05:35.812
[gasps]

00:05:35.986 --> 00:05:37.553
What are you guys
all staring at?

00:05:37.727 --> 00:05:39.729
♪ ♪

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.037
Oh!

00:05:44.211 --> 00:05:45.909
Mom!

00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:47.389
Your hair.

00:05:47.563 --> 00:05:49.434
It's massive and wild,
and I love it.

00:05:49.608 --> 00:05:51.175
Thanks.

00:05:51.349 --> 00:05:53.482
Gran, your hair!

00:05:53.656 --> 00:05:55.484
What? It's temporary.

00:05:55.658 --> 00:05:58.095
No. It's flying this way.

00:06:00.576 --> 00:06:02.491
[squawks]

00:06:02.665 --> 00:06:03.796
[screeches]

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.538
Wigasus has returned!

00:06:06.712 --> 00:06:08.497
-Get off me.
-[sloths cheer]

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.892
-Uh-huh. Uh-huh.
-[squeaking chatter]

00:06:13.066 --> 00:06:14.198
Get to the point.

00:06:14.372 --> 00:06:15.678
Punch monkeys.

00:06:15.852 --> 00:06:17.941
I hate punch monkeys.

00:06:18.115 --> 00:06:22.206
Wigasus says the men have been
taken over yonder.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.208
-[Wigasus squeaks]
-[thunder cracks]

00:06:24.382 --> 00:06:26.079
Great. What's the plan?

00:06:26.253 --> 00:06:28.995
What would
the Thunder Sisters do?

00:06:29.169 --> 00:06:30.170
Aw.

00:06:30.344 --> 00:06:32.216
All right, Thunder Sisters!

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:33.739
If we're gonna rescue these men,

00:06:33.913 --> 00:06:36.525
there's something
we're gonna need.

00:06:36.699 --> 00:06:37.743
-A window?
-No.

00:06:37.917 --> 00:06:39.179
-A catchy chant?
-No!

00:06:39.353 --> 00:06:40.920
BOTH:
Each other.

00:06:41.094 --> 00:06:42.966
"Each" what? No!

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:44.968
New tribe names.

00:06:45.142 --> 00:06:48.014
Sandy, you shall be
called "Seeker."

00:06:48.188 --> 00:06:49.755
Eep, "Fire Heart."

00:06:49.929 --> 00:06:51.496
Ugga, "Blood Horn."

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:52.932
Thunk, you're... "Thunk."

00:06:53.106 --> 00:06:54.543
[growls]

00:06:54.717 --> 00:06:56.153
Smart girl whose name
I don't remember...

00:06:56.327 --> 00:06:57.502
-I'm Dawn.
-No!

00:06:57.676 --> 00:06:59.548
You are "Sister Sunset."

00:06:59.722 --> 00:07:02.376
And you are "Bog Water."

00:07:02.551 --> 00:07:04.335
My name's "Bog Water"?

00:07:04.509 --> 00:07:06.076
I thought of it
before you had cool hair.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.949
I am Bog Water!

00:07:10.123 --> 00:07:11.385
Hey, Sister Sunset.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.909
Yeah, Fire Heart?

00:07:13.083 --> 00:07:14.911
-You see those wolf spiders?
-Yeah.

00:07:15.085 --> 00:07:16.695
-Want to ride 'em?
-Yeah!

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:17.914
Thunder Sisters.

00:07:18.088 --> 00:07:20.133
-Thunder Sisters!
-Thunder Sisters!

00:07:20.307 --> 00:07:21.352
Thunder Sister!

00:07:21.526 --> 00:07:23.049
[both shouting]

00:07:23.223 --> 00:07:25.487
ALL:
Thunder Sisters!

00:07:25.661 --> 00:07:28.490
[all whooping]

00:07:28.664 --> 00:07:30.666
♪ ♪

00:07:39.631 --> 00:07:41.590
[wild laughter,
chatter, whooping]

